"h307": "Archives: <code>/data/graylog-archives</code> (any mounted path)",
"h308": "Logs: <code>journalctl -u jt-glogarch -f</code>",
"h309": "Upgrade",
"h31": "OpenSearch, client certificates only",
"h310": "Upgrades are designed to keep the data, keep the service usable and keep scheduled archiving running; each release is tested against state written by older ones.",
"h311": "An Ubuntu 22.04 → 24.04 upgrade underneath is handled: the steps before the reinstall need only bash and Python's standard library",
"h312": "Stopped at <code>Not possible to fast-forward</code>? See the FAQ in the README: one <code>git reset</code> fixes clones made before 2026-09-13",
"h313": "Closed networks",
"h314": "Build a bundle where there is internet access and carry it in: the program, every dependency wheel and the PDF engine's browser, installed with no network at all.",
"h315": "The bundle carries its own SBOM with a SHA-256 for every file",
"h316": "It cannot carry the operating system libraries Chromium needs (libnss3, libgbm1…); the installer tells you which are missing",
"h317": "Step-by-step setup, every setting and the FAQ are in the README:",
"h318": "Install, upgrade and closed networks",
